hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1419","Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban Al-Masry told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Ismail bin Rabi’ah bin Hisham bin Ishaq told us On the authority of Amer bin Luay al-Madini, that he heard his grandfather Hisham bin Ishaq speaking, on the authority of his father Ishaq bin Abdullah, that Al-Walid bin Utba, the Emir of Medina, sent him to Ibn Abbas, and he said: O son of my brother, ask him how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did in raining on the day of rain. Did he ask people for water? Ishaq said: So I went to Ibn Abbas and said: O Abu Abbas, how did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do with rain rain on the day of rain? Did he drink water? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, humbled and reveling, and he did what he did during Breakfast and Eid al-Adha.”"
